00:04:05,714 --> 00:04:11,714
You know the drill!

2
00:08:11,428 --> 00:08:17,428
Slumber Party Massacre is a horror, comedy film directed by Danishka Esterhazy.

3
00:12:17,142 --> 00:12:23,142
Dana, daughter of the only survivor of a massacre in 1993,
is going on a weekend trip with her friends.

4
00:16:22,857 --> 00:16:28,857
After their car breaks down in the very same town where her mother once fought the Driller Killer, Dana and her
friends must come face-to-face with the man who has haunted her mother’s life for the past 30 years.

5
00:20:28,571 --> 00:20:34,571
Dana Devereaux, played by Hannah Gonera.

6
00:24:34,285 --> 00:24:40,285
Maeve, played by Frances Sholto-Douglas.

7
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Alix, played by Mila Rayne.

8
00:32:45,714 --> 00:32:51,714
Breanie, played by Alex McGregor.

9
00:36:51,428 --> 00:36:57,428
Ashley, played by Reze-Tiana Wessels.

10
00:40:57,142 --> 00:41:03,142
Russ Thorne, played by Rob van Vuuren.

11
00:45:02,857 --> 00:45:08,857
Slumber Party Massacre is a 2021 slasher film directed by
Danishka Esterhazy and written by Suzanne Keilly.

12
00:49:08,571 --> 00:49:14,571
It is described as a "modern reimagining" of and stand-alone sequel to the original 1982 film The
Slumber Party Massacre, and the fourth film released in the overall Massacre franchise.

13
00:53:14,285 --> 00:53:20,285
It stars Hannah Gonera, Frances Sholto-Douglas, Alex McGregor, Mila Rayne, Reze-Tiana
Wessels with Schelaine Bennett, Rob van Vuuren and Jennifer Steyn.

14
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
It follows a girls' slumber party which becomes a bloodbath when an
escaped mental patient arrives with a power drill.

15
01:01:25,714 --> 01:01:31,714
Studios announced a remake of the film to be helmed by director
Danishka Esterhazy and written by Suzanne Keilly.

16
01:05:31,428 --> 01:05:37,428
Production began in Stellenbosch, South Africa in March
2021, with the cast being announced in April.

17
01:09:37,142 --> 01:09:43,142
Slumber Party Massacre made its world premiere at the Fantastic Fest in Austin, Texas
on September 27, 2021, and was released on Syfy Channel on October 16.

18
01:13:42,857 --> 01:13:48,857
The film received generally positive reviews from critics, with praise for its feminist themes, gore and the
performances of the cast, but criticism for its screenplay, character development and pacing.

19
01:17:48,571 --> 01:17:54,571
The film explores themes of slumber party,
sleepover, remake, murder, serial killer.

20
01:21:54,285 --> 01:22:00,285
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
